#ASSERT `Art 65(6) representatives of the advisory forum may be invited to the sub-groups as observers` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 65(6) representatives of the advisory forum may be invited to the sub-groups as observers` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Art 65(6) representatives of the advisory forum may be invited to the sub-groups as observers` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the Guide's periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b), says of a "where ..." condition: "when it fails the answer is `JUST FALSE`", and "Where appropriate" opens this sentence, so the Guide's line gives `JUST FALSE` and not `NOTHING` when it is not appropriate to invite them; the earlier `NOTHING` rested on reading the grant as limited in its own wording, which the Guide's line on a "where" condition does not support
#ASSERT `Art 65(6) representatives of the advisory forum may be invited to the sub-groups as observers` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
